            <ArticleTitle>Dissociation between cutaneous and deep sensibility in central post-stroke pain (CPSP).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>331-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present three cases of central post-stroke pain after right hemorrhagic or ischemic stroke associated with severe impairment of cutaneous sensibility but preservation of stimulus-evoked pain from periosteum. This is the first such report of dissociation of cutaneous- from deep-tissue sensibility loss.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
